# Personal knowledge base (`docs/ai/`)

This repo has a **local** Cursor development knowledge base at `docs/ai/` (gitignored). Official shareable docs stay in `docs/zh/`.

This Cursor-local memory is separate from any external cross-project/long-term KB. Do not redirect or replace `docs/ai/` with the external KB.

## Cold start (every new Cursor chat that touches this project)

1. Read `docs/ai/HANDOFF.md`
2. Read `docs/ai/META/phases.md` and `docs/ai/META/preferences.md`
3. Read the active topic under the current phase (`INDEX.md`, `QA.md`)

## Auto-record

Write/update `docs/ai/` when any of these happen:

- Milestone conclusion (design, investigation, implementation chunk)
- User corrects architecture/preferences/口径
- User asks a project-development “I don’t understand / need to review later” question → append current topic `QA.md`
- Important pitfall or decision, especially evolution between approaches/runs
- Phase change → update `META/phases.md` + refresh `HANDOFF.md`
- Long Cursor session ending or context about to compact → flush first

## Structure rules

- Use phase dirs: `00-pre-dev/`, `01-dev/`, `02-post-dev/`, `experiments/`
- Per topic/run: `SUMMARY.md`, `EVOLUTION.md`, `QA.md` as needed
- Experiments: use the project’s established evaluation convention and preserve evaluate output
- Keep code in normal repo paths; keep local development records and result artifacts in `docs/ai/`

## Handoff

After meaningful progress, ensure `docs/ai/HANDOFF.md` lets a new Cursor Agent continue the development process without this chat’s context.

